# GitHub Flow

Follow [GitHub Flow](https://docs.github.com/en/get-started/using-github/github-flow) for all changes. There is no `develop` integration branch.

## Branches
- **main** — protected; the only long-lived branch; merge only via PR
- **feature/** — new work (`feature/123-short-description`)
- **hotfix/** — urgent fix branched from `main` (`hotfix/critical-bug`)

## Rules
1. Never commit directly to **main** — use a branch and PR
2. Branch from **main**
3. Keep PRs focused; one concern per branch where practical
4. Use clear commit messages; PR title summarizes the change
5. Do not push secrets; use user secrets, GitHub secrets, or env vars

## CI / CD
- **Src CI** (`*-src-ci.yml`) runs on pull requests **into `main`**, using the PR head (path-filtered). Required checks on `main` must pass before merge. Temporary: also `workflow_dispatch` — remove when Azure settings testing is done ([issue 116](https://github.com/dertinfo/dertinfo-mono/issues/116)).
- **Src CD** (`*-src-cd.yml`) and **infra CD** (`*-infra-cd.yml`) run on **push to `main`** after merge. App/infra CD uses GitHub Environments `development` then gated `production`. Src CD also has temporary `workflow_dispatch` (`dev-only` / `full`); infra CD keeps `workflow_dispatch` for Bicep re-runs.

## Agent workflow
- Before git work: confirm the branch is based on **main**
- Create/switch to an appropriately named branch before edits
- Summarize impacted apps in PR description (`apps/dert-api`, etc.)
- Include a change log in the PR in nearly all cases. If unsure whether to leave it off, ask first. See [change logs](changelogs.mdc).
